{#
  Foot of a customer mail (block GARAN, part 2, L2): who sends it — firm and
  legal form, address, and the operator's footer from the shop configuration,
  the one the invoice prints. Consho adds no legal wording of its own.

  BELOW the white column, on the grey ground: included in the outer cell, after the
  600 px table, and as wide as it. Variable: frame {company, address, footer,
  logo} — or null.
#}
{% if frame|default(null) and (frame.company or frame.address or frame.footer) %}
<table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding: 16px 28px 0 28px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #666666;">
{% if frame.company %}<p style="margin: 0;">{{ frame.company }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if frame.address %}<p style="margin: 0;">{{ frame.address }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if frame.footer %}<p style="margin: 8px 0 0 0;">{{ frame.footer|nl2br }}</p>{% endif %}
</td></tr>
</table>
{% endif %}
